PL011 UART — QEMU virt console
==============================

The QEMU virt machine wires a PrimeCell PL011 UART at `0x09000000`
as its primary console. QEMU's firmware leaves the device already
initialised, so this module only needs the bare minimum: poll the
TX-FIFO-full flag in `UARTFR` and stuff bytes into `UARTDR`.

    module oskit.arch.aarch64.board.virt

PL011 register addresses.

    val UART0_DR: i64 = 0x09000000
    val UART0_FR: i64 = 0x09000018
    val UARTFR_TXFF = 0x20

Write one byte to the data register, waiting for the TX FIFO to
drain first. `volatile` on the flag pointer keeps the read from
being hoisted out of the busy-wait loop by the optimiser.

    uart_putc(c: int)
        volatile var fr: *i32 = *i32(UART0_FR)
        var busy = 1
        while busy != 0
            busy = int(*fr) & UARTFR_TXFF
        var dr: *i32 = *i32(UART0_DR)
        *dr = i32(c)

Write a NUL-terminated sysl string, translating `'\n'` into CRLF
for terminal emulators that expect carriage returns.

    uart_puts(s: string)
        val p = *byte(s)
        val n = len(s)
        for var i = 0; i < n; i++
            val ch = int(p[i])
            if ch == 10
                uart_putc(13)
            uart_putc(ch)
